Fillets: a walked blend whose contact on one face runs into the face at an
end of the spine before that end is cut by that face, up to where its
other contact reaches it (mitcad#121), as 0059 does for analytic blends:
e.g. the rounding of an inside corner between a wall and the rounded top
edge of another wall, where the first wall's contact leaves it across its
top edge before the corner's edge reaches the top.

- ChFi3d_Builder::WalkedCutToEnd, called by PerformSetOfSurf for each end
  of an open spine once the stripe is walked: where the stripe stops short
  of the end vertex V with the contact on face N on an edge E of N, the
  face B across E holds V and is not tangent to N, and the other contact
  (on face Fo) is inside its face, the blend is walked on from the
  stripe's end section with N's surface unbounded (a face of N's surface
  without edges) and Fo as it is, until the other contact reaches the
  edge Eq between Fo and B at V. That piece is cut by B
  (ChFi3d_KPartCutPiece, as over a hole): its side on N becomes the cut
  of the blend by B, from the point on E to the point Q on Eq where the
  blend ends in a point. The spine's end becomes a free boundary with a
  singular extremity (as in ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd): no corner is made at V.
  Before, OCCT's corner at V intersected the blend with B from the
  stripe's end; where Fo is tangent to B at V this gave an invalid result
  (an open wire on Fo, a self-intersecting wire on the blend) or failed.
- ChFi3d_KPartLineParam: on a bounded line (a walked blend's contact) that
  has no foot of the point, the end of the line nearer to it.
